   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">PRO-R15: Number of children that received support specified to their needs</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) This indicator covers response to children (girls and boys under 18). 2) Appropriate response is defined as the provision of comprehensive services/assistance based on a thorough analysis of the risks faced by persons. The protection outcome of the response must be well defined. Relevant SOPs (including functional Referral Mechanism) should be followed. 3) Use the activity description field to to describe what services (medical, MHPSS, legal, security, etc.), as well as SOPs are in place. Activities can include psychosocial support to children, Child Friendly Spaces and support to parents to fulfill their protection responsibilities towards their children.</narrative>
    </description>
